{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1543967-regaining-legend-while-imbuing","id":1543967,"title":"Regaining Legend while Imbuing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-16T03:13:54-07:00","id":1543967,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Regaining Legend while Imbuing","content":"Hello<br /> <br /> Here's some thoughts I had.<br /> <br /> I'm in the process of reading through Scion 2nd Edition again, currently finished Boons in Hero. As a former 1st Edition player, the changes to the amount and regain of Legend points still feels weird to me, even though I see the difference between &quot;spend Legend&quot; and &quot;imbue Legend&quot;. My head is convinced, that this system works, especially, as often Legend costs are omitted, if it's all trivial targets.<br /> <br /> But as I've read through the Boons, there were some, where you imbue Legend to inflict a Condition/Enhancement/Complication on a target. And for my understanding, if the description doesn't say something else, then this stays as long, as I imbue the Legend point. Ok, makes sense. I weave some of my divine power into the feeling of drowning (Water Boon &quot;Sink Hopes&quot;, Hero p. 263) and put it on the (non-trivial) leader of a Yakuza gang, that likes to drown shopkeepers who won't pay their protection money. This is a punishment, which I will lift in the near future, once we dealt with him. Maybe a bit longer, if I'm a vengeful fella.<br /> <br /> Increasing the Enhancement of my Katana by <b>Appeasing the Kami</b> (Yaoyorozu-No-Kamigami, Hero p. 265), so I have an edge in combat sounds good. Maybe I use this Boon before entering dangerous territory and regain it, when the dust has settled.<br /> <br /> But what about something meant to be more permanent? <b>Divine Providence</b> (Prosperity, Hero p. 259) for example. I bless my Cult with it, as they are very dear to me, and don't want to end it anytime soon. I &quot;loose&quot; a point of Legend and won't be able to get it back without refusing the blessing of my Cult? Well...Maybe it's just how I apparently set my priorites and if blessing my Cult with prosperity is what I want, then it's my decission.<br /> <br /> Then I read <b>Lay Geis</b> (Geasa, Hero p. 271) and to me it seems, laying Geasa on people is a usual thing for the Tuatha to do and I'm not sure how common it is, to lift them. Does it mean, the Tuatha are always short of some Legend points, imbued in some Geasa? I can't really believe it. Maybe things change on Demigod or God Tier. I think I heard something of Demigods not needing to pay Legend costs on trivial targets, even if the Boon does not explicitly says so. So maybe I'm just not far enough into the books for this to make sense for me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But now to my actual question<br /> <br /> I then reread the section about regaining spent Legend points from Fatebindings and sacrifices. There I noticed that if my Legend pool is full, once I complete a sacrifice, I can spend or imbue the gained Legend point directly in a Boon or Marvel. So...Does that mean, the amount of Legend points in my pool and the points of my Legend imbued somewhere combined can exceed the size of my Legend pool?<br /> Circling back to <b>Divine Providence</b> as a Legend 2 Scion. I bless my Cult by imbuing one point of Legend, leaving me with one point left in my pool to use while adventuring with my Band. Over the course of play, I don't spend Legend, just imbuing it and regaining it, as effects end. Then I accept a new Fatebinding, refilling my pool to two points. Now my character has 2/2 Legend points in their pool and another imbued to ensure the wellbeing of my cult. Is this assumption right?<br /> Would this also allow me to use this imbued Legend points as some sort of supply in dire circumstances? Enabling my Prosperity Scion to draw on three Legend points to spend, when facing off against a deadly foe, at the cost of his blessing? To me it seems very in line with the theme of divine beings' blessings tied to the power of that being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12016-echsenkoenig","name":"Echsenkoenig","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T15:37:32-07:00","id":1544028,"title":"","content":"I'm also learning the system so I don't have an official rule for you but my impression is that you're limited to recovering points that are spent, not imbued. If I am wrong I will be glad to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T08:56:46-07:00","id":1544464,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. Imbued points don't technically leave your pool; they're just busy doing something (whatever they're Imbued into) and can't be accessed to do other things without canceling the Imbuement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T09:37:26-07:00","id":1544469,"title":"","content":"Ok...That was, what I assumed at first.<br /> But it collides with the description about sacrifices with a full pool. If I was only able to directly <b>spend</b> the point of Legend gained, everything was in line with that. But it says I can also <b>imbue</b> it. Leaving me with 2/2 Legend points in my pool and 1 point imbued, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12016-echsenkoenig","name":"Echsenkoenig","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T14:31:55-07:00","id":1544503,"title":"","content":"Note that Lay Geis involves<i> spending </i>Legend, not <i>investing</i> it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T18:34:09-07:00","id":1544617,"title":"","content":"I'd be inclined to rule that a Legend over your Maximum that you imbue in something will stay there until the end of the session, until the end of it's duration, or until you chose to end it, whichever comes first. My inclination is that it only &quot;works&quot; for the Boon or Marvel you've Imbued, and if you end it you don't get the Legend back -- you got that legend specifically for the Boon or Marvel you're powering.<br /> <br /> But this is my inclination as a Storyguide, and the rules aren't entirely clear either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}